<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuela disclosed a $237.5 billion debt pile and is moving toward a large restructuring while the United States signed a military cooperation pact with the interim Venezuelan government, after which a U.S. marine died falling overboard during a Caribbean operation linked to the renewed ties. Senate investigations target JD Vance for allegedly steering a Venezuelan oil license to Vitol and a separate probe examines another senator’s role in the same deal, while Citi considers re-entering the market after a five-year exit and the pact was later declared null and void by Venezuelan authorities. Illegal gold mining continues, and Eni and Repsol pledged $2 billion in joint-venture investments. According to UCDP, there were 2 battle-related deaths in 2007.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxOakxRRS1xODNKVEMzdlowcjUzd2g4amNoV0JSSzdQc0JEUXg1WWxSbGxOaGhYWDZWSlQzeldBelpvUnpXb3g3bHdMUWd4NWhiZFJRZnEtSWU4TDBXS0Q1Q21CWE9QUkxkT2YxYVI5MzlJNkVJS3FRZ3NuMG90Y0JBMFNKRGEtOEhlOUktTVJwU2hoSHVVVW56NXI0ZlZIOHo3TGt0UTc3VnA4VlV5MGZoTmlfS05qQlpQcWpiUWNtSjI?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxPX3RKNmswZ0hZN0VZTXhBd1Q2bTg4clBBaWZhSXA4N1pHNEZrd3hLNlNRTGR1RnV3MUQ3dXIwYVZ0SXNwZVFkZGFsMmdSR3ZKSi1oUmZhenE2ZS11X2RENzZXWnEtbHU3ckc0NlNCR2Vrc0JqczlSYXdjUHBTSmV1dmliNThwSlZ4SEtJ?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMib0FVX3lxTE93QlBzMm9LcGI3UWFHOEhfaW5MYlRtazNmODJZWl9mN3lBS3NDb1NUWTNPLTFodXBLM2lMWlZHYW9KQ3gxelBJTzdqdTR6emtuZ0g4ZnJCX0MxVDBiWWpIRGNMUTBOVEJNZEMzUDhJOA?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuwFBVV95cUxOUEEwU0d6SzJSRFZ6c1VBWmRoVFJjMDVOMS1ZUFU4ZGVlZG44bkRxQ3RaZk92b1V0dWdpQzhVemVSdGJLcVo5VVhwT3F1c3F3Ti1FUF85eTVEUlY4MU04cWZZa